  "conversionNotes": [
    "Trip Wire trigger: 'On a score of 3+' on D6 -> 5+ on D12.",
    "Master Trapper skill: traps triggered on 2+ -> 3+ (printed in skill text, not copied into fighter rules since it is a skill).",
    "Infiltrator 'roll a D6 for each, lowest sets up first' changed to D12 (no threshold).",
    "Skill table column 'Special' = Horned Hunter special skills (Master Trapper, Infiltration, Foul Odour, Animal Friendship, Pathfinder, Hide in Shadows). Priest of Taal has no Shooting column; Initiates and Horned Hunter have no Academic.",
    "Prayers of Taal difficulties are printed as on a D6 table with difficulty values (5-9) and were left unchanged.",
    "Hero list vs henchman list: Horned Hunter, Priest, Initiates use the main list; Zealots and Drunken Gang use the henchmen list. Hunting arrows, Blessed Stag Hide and Trip wire are listed as misc; Blessed Stag Hide 'Rare 10' and Trip Wire 'Common' availability recorded in notes.",
    "Max 12 warriors. Drunken Gang and Warhounds are 0-5 each; Zealots unlimited."
  ]
